<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH KOMERCNI LOWERS REFERENCE RATE 80BPS.</title>
<headline>CZECH KOMERCNI LOWERS REFERENCE RATE 80BPS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The largest Czech commercial bank, Komercni Banka a.s., said on Thursday it was lowering its key lending rate, the reference rate, 80 basis points to 15.6 percent, effective on Friday.</p>
<p>The reference rate, which shadows the Prague interbank six-month offered rate (PRIBOR), is used for aligning the whole of Komercni's lending schedule. It said its base rate would be lowered to 13.90 percent on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
